# Copy to ~/.config/polytoken-container.env and fill in.
# Passed into the container via --env-file at launch. NEVER baked into the image.
#
# Add whatever provider keys your Polytoken providers read from the environment:

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Examples of others you might need:
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# ---- Discord bridge connector auto-start (optional) ----
# When BRIDGE_RELAY_TOKEN is present, the bridge-connector-autostart session_start
# hook auto-starts the Discord bridge connector inside this container (fail-open:
# never blocks the session). Most values are auto-derived by the launcher;
# only the relay token is required here. See BRIDGE_RELAY_ADDRESS below.
#
# BRIDGE_RELAY_TOKEN=<shared relay token, same as ~/.config/polytoken-discord.env on the Mac>
#
# One literal URL is used for both the host (BRIDGE_RELAY_ADVERTISE) and the
# container (BRIDGE_RELAY_ADDRESS). ws://host.docker.internal:8765 is the
# default; use ws://host.containers.internal:8765 where podman resolves that
# name instead. Do not mix the two.
# BRIDGE_RELAY_ADDRESS=ws://host.docker.internal:8765
# BRIDGE_RELAY_ADVERTISE=ws://host.docker.internal:8765
#
# Optional overrides (rarely needed):
# BRIDGE_CONNECTOR_ID=            # deterministic per container; default bridge-<hostname>
# BRIDGE_CONTAINER_ID=            # default hostname
# BRIDGE_CONNECTOR_PYTHON=        # absolute python to use instead of the connector venv
# BRIDGE_VENV_DIR=                # connector venv; default /home/dev/.local/share/polytoken/bridge/venv
# BRIDGE_REPO_DIR=/Users/gfranks/workspace/discord-pt-stream
#
# Token rotation: update BOTH this file and the Mac host's ~/.config/polytoken-discord.env,
# kickstart the launchd agent (local.polytoken-discord-bridge), and relaunch a container
# session (the container side has no hot path — it reads this file only at launch).
